WEBVTT


00:01:12.080 --> 00:01:15.117
We are gathered here today
to immortalise in song


00:01:15.240 --> 00:01:18.516
the life and untimely death
of a great legend.


00:01:18.640 --> 00:01:20.870
- Rango.
- So sit back, relax,


00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:24.709
and enjoy your low-calorie popcorn
and assorted confections


00:01:24.840 --> 00:01:29.391
while we tell you the strange
and bewildering tale of a hero


00:01:29.520 --> 00:01:32.796
who has yet to enter his own story.


00:01:46.920 --> 00:01:49.514
Crunchy, creamy, cookie,
candy, cupcake.


00:01:50.800 --> 00:01:52.870
Okay, everybody,
let's take it from the top.


00:01:54.200 --> 00:01:57.476
The stage is set,
the night moist with apprehension.


00:01:57.600 --> 00:02:01.388
Alone in her chamber, the princess
prepares to take her own life.


00:02:02.120 --> 00:02:05.795
"It is far better to nourish worms
than to live without love."


00:02:05.920 --> 00:02:07.751
She reaches for the poisoned chalice.


00:02:07.880 --> 00:02:11.031
Meanwhile, the wicked Malvolio
plots his ascension to the throne


00:02:11.560 --> 00:02:13.437
while her ageing father lies gravely ill.


00:02:13.960 --> 00:02:15.996
"Yes, I am gravely ill."


00:02:17.240 --> 00:02:19.196
"Hark, who goes there?"


00:02:19.480 --> 00:02:21.755
'Tis I, the much-anticipated hero,


00:02:21.880 --> 00:02:24.394
returning to rescue
his emotionally unstable maiden!


00:02:24.520 --> 00:02:26.431
Unhand her, you jailers of virtue,


00:02:26.560 --> 00:02:29.279
or taste the bitter sting
of my vengeance!


00:02:30.320 --> 00:02:32.151
The sting of my...


00:02:34.720 --> 00:02:35.914
Dr Marx?


00:02:36.040 --> 00:02:38.554
Dr Marx,
I'm not getting anything from you.


00:02:38.680 --> 00:02:42.389
People, we've talked about this.
Acting is reacting.


00:02:42.520 --> 00:02:44.875
Victor, you were wooden!
There, I said it.


00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:46.718
Mr Timms? You were good.


00:02:48.160 --> 00:02:49.752
Perhaps a little too good.


00:02:50.280 --> 00:02:53.909
What's that, Victor? My character's
undefined? That's absurd.


00:02:54.040 --> 00:02:58.795
I know who I am.
I'm the guy, the protagonist, the hero.


00:02:58.920 --> 00:03:02.674
Every story needs a hero.
I mean, who else is better qualified


00:03:02.800 --> 00:03:06.270
to bask in the adulation
of his numerous companions?


00:03:24.520 --> 00:03:26.317
<i>The stage is waiting.</i>


00:03:26.760 --> 00:03:29.320
<i>The audience thirsts for adventure.</i>


00:03:31.560 --> 00:03:33.039
<i>Who am I?</i>


00:03:34.040 --> 00:03:35.473
<i>I could be anyone.</i>


00:03:35.960 --> 00:03:40.192
I could be the sea cap'n
returning from a mighty voyage


00:03:40.320 --> 00:03:42.390
to reclaim his mechanical arm!


00:03:43.880 --> 00:03:47.793
Or I could be the rogue anthropologist,
battling pythons down in the Congo!


00:03:47.920 --> 00:03:49.558
Down, Chongo, down!


00:03:50.320 --> 00:03:52.436
And if you desire romance,


00:03:53.840 --> 00:03:56.877
I will become the greatest lover
the world has ever known!


00:04:03.520 --> 00:04:07.479
I couldn't help but notice you
noticing me noticing you.


00:04:07.600 --> 00:04:11.149
You know, the womens find me
uncomfortably good looking.


00:04:11.280 --> 00:04:13.589
But you seem remarkably at ease.


00:04:14.080 --> 00:04:15.798
Stop it. No, really.


00:04:15.920 --> 00:04:18.195
Well, if you must. What are you doing?


00:04:18.320 --> 00:04:20.197
That tickles. Are those real?


00:04:21.280 --> 00:04:23.350
That's it! Conflict.


00:04:23.480 --> 00:04:25.869
Victor, you were right.
I have been undefined.


00:04:26.720 --> 00:04:30.872
People, I've had an epiphany.
The hero cannot exist in a vacuum!


00:04:31.080 --> 00:04:33.958
What our story needs is an ironic,
unexpected event


00:04:34.080 --> 00:04:36.719
that will propel the hero into conflict!


00:05:31.000 --> 00:05:32.035
Mr Timms?


00:06:11.680 --> 00:06:13.557
That's right! You!


00:06:14.920 --> 00:06:16.797
Don't be shy. Come on.


00:06:17.240 --> 00:06:18.912
It's okay.


00:06:19.040 --> 00:06:20.917
That's it, a little closer.


00:06:22.400 --> 00:06:23.469
Good.


00:06:24.000 --> 00:06:25.672
I won't bite you.


00:06:27.840 --> 00:06:29.637
I need a little help here.


00:06:30.280 --> 00:06:31.429
Are you okay?


00:06:32.080 --> 00:06:34.435
I must get to the other side.


00:06:34.560 --> 00:06:37.199
The other side? You mean, just now,
that was you crossing the road?


00:06:37.320 --> 00:06:38.514
That's why the...


00:06:39.680 --> 00:06:40.829
Why'd you do that?


00:06:40.960 --> 00:06:43.918
This is my quest. He waits for me.


00:06:44.040 --> 00:06:45.314
What? Who?


00:06:45.440 --> 00:06:48.830
The Spirit of the West,
<i>amigo.</i> The one.


00:06:48.960 --> 00:06:53.112
They say he rides an alabaster carriage
with golden guardians to protect him.


00:06:53.240 --> 00:06:54.912
What are you talking about?


00:06:55.040 --> 00:06:58.237
Enlightenment.
We are nothing without it.


00:06:58.760 --> 00:07:01.797
Nothing? Your delusional quest
just ruined my life!


00:07:01.920 --> 00:07:04.229
I had an incredibly complex
social network going!


00:07:04.360 --> 00:07:07.079
Highly sophisticated friends!
I was very popular!


00:07:07.200 --> 00:07:09.191
Friends? I don't see no friends.


00:07:11.560 --> 00:07:12.549
You are a very lonely lizard.


00:07:14.840 --> 00:07:18.913
Now help me up
and I will help you find what you seek.


00:07:19.040 --> 00:07:21.998
- You will?
- Quickly. I must get back to my quest.


00:07:22.120 --> 00:07:25.476
- You mean you've done this before?
- Yes. Many times.


00:07:26.160 --> 00:07:28.913
Come, come. That's it, pull my finger.


00:07:29.040 --> 00:07:30.917
The Spirit is waiting for me.


00:07:31.320 --> 00:07:32.673
Okay, okay.


00:07:37.920 --> 00:07:39.831
Okay. That's not going to work.


00:07:39.960 --> 00:07:40.915
I must get to the other side.


00:07:42.720 --> 00:07:45.188
Why don't you just wait
until there are no cars coming?


00:07:45.320 --> 00:07:46.878
It's not so easy as it looks.


00:07:47.000 --> 00:07:47.955
What?


00:07:48.240 --> 00:07:49.389
Is a metaphor.


00:08:18.760 --> 00:08:19.795
There's another one!


00:08:21.640 --> 00:08:22.595
I knew it.


00:08:33.760 --> 00:08:35.432
You need a little help, <i>amigo?</i>


00:08:35.560 --> 00:08:38.438
I think the metaphor broke my spleen.


00:08:38.560 --> 00:08:40.994
The path to knowledge
is fraught with consequence.


00:08:41.120 --> 00:08:43.793
I'm just looking for the path to water.


00:08:43.920 --> 00:08:48.391
If you want to find water,
you must first find Dirt.


00:08:49.560 --> 00:08:50.788
Dirt.


00:08:51.600 --> 00:08:53.909
Destiny, she is kind to you.


00:08:54.040 --> 00:08:56.793
Tomorrow is Wednesday.
The water comes.


00:08:57.800 --> 00:09:01.190
At noon, the townspeople gather
for a mysterious ritual.


00:09:02.440 --> 00:09:05.955
A town? You mean, with real people
and everything? Where?


00:09:06.080 --> 00:09:08.753
A day's journey. Follow your shadow.


00:09:10.520 --> 00:09:13.796
You want me to just walk out
into the desert?


00:09:13.920 --> 00:09:14.909
That's the way.


00:09:15.040 --> 00:09:17.349
Okay. So you're saying


00:09:17.480 --> 00:09:20.836
there's a town, a real town,
not a metaphor town.


00:09:20.960 --> 00:09:22.359
Go on. It's okay.


00:09:22.920 --> 00:09:23.955
Okay.


00:09:24.640 --> 00:09:25.959
Well, then, I'm going.


00:09:26.560 --> 00:09:29.279
I am leaving the road now!


00:09:29.840 --> 00:09:32.673
I'm walking into the desert!


00:09:33.280 --> 00:09:34.395
Alone!


00:09:34.520 --> 00:09:36.954
We all have our journeys to make!


00:09:37.640 --> 00:09:40.108
I will see you on the other side.


00:09:53.720 --> 00:09:56.678
<i>Welcome,</i> amigo


00:09:56.800 --> 00:09:59.633
<i>To the land without end</i>


00:10:00.160 --> 00:10:02.799
<i>The desert and death</i>


00:10:02.920 --> 00:10:06.629
<i>Are the closest of friends</i>


00:10:06.760 --> 00:10:09.513
<i>We sing of his courage</i>


00:10:09.640 --> 00:10:12.677
<i>In magnificent song</i>


00:10:12.800 --> 00:10:15.473
<i>But pay close attention</i>


00:10:15.600 --> 00:10:18.353
<i>He won't be here long</i>


00:10:22.520 --> 00:10:25.512
<i>As the birds pluck his eyes</i>
<i>The sun bleaches his bones</i>


00:10:25.640 --> 00:10:30.350
<i>See his entrails get scattered</i>
<i>Watch him lose his</i> cojones


00:10:36.760 --> 00:10:38.910
Here in the Mojave Desert,


00:10:39.040 --> 00:10:44.034
animals have had millions of years
to adapt to the harsh environment.


00:10:44.160 --> 00:10:47.232
But the lizard? He is going to die.


00:10:48.000 --> 00:10:50.833
"Four score and seven years ago,
our fathers..."


00:10:50.960 --> 00:10:52.916
- Don't move.
- What?


00:10:58.720 --> 00:11:00.517
- Don't move!
- Not moving.


00:11:00.640 --> 00:11:01.629
Not moving.


00:11:01.760 --> 00:11:03.830
Try to blend in.


00:11:03.960 --> 00:11:05.439
Blend in? What do you mean?


00:11:09.080 --> 00:11:10.229
Blend in.


00:11:10.360 --> 00:11:11.998
What are you saying?


00:11:13.760 --> 00:11:15.239
- Too late.
- No, no. It's not too late!


00:11:15.360 --> 00:11:17.476
I'm blending! I'm a blender!


00:11:17.800 --> 00:11:19.597
Hey, calm down! What are you doing?


00:11:22.640 --> 00:11:23.868
Stop moving!


00:11:24.520 --> 00:11:26.112
Try not to look conspicuous.


00:11:35.440 --> 00:11:36.714
- What are you doing?
- I'm blending.


00:11:36.840 --> 00:11:38.558
- Go blend somewhere else.
- Don't distract me.


00:11:38.680 --> 00:11:40.398
- No room at the inn.
- It's an art, not a science.


00:11:40.520 --> 00:11:42.351
- Find your own hiding place.
- No, this is good.


00:11:42.960 --> 00:11:45.030
Here she comes! You better run, Mojito!


00:11:45.160 --> 00:11:48.755
- What? I thought you said, "Don't move."
- That was before. Now, you run.


00:12:34.240 --> 00:12:36.117
Oh, hey. Proboscis.


00:12:36.800 --> 00:12:37.755
Testy.


00:12:50.240 --> 00:12:53.915
Please, no, please. I have vertigo!
My glands are swelling!


00:12:55.400 --> 00:12:56.469
Please, no.


00:13:04.560 --> 00:13:07.950
You! I'll kill you! You stupid lizard!


00:13:08.080 --> 00:13:09.877
Get out of there.
I'm going to strangle your <i>huevos!</i>


00:13:10.000 --> 00:13:11.672
Big bird! Big bird!


00:13:12.560 --> 00:13:15.120
No, wait! Come back! I was just kidding!


00:13:15.240 --> 00:13:17.037
- Come on, we're friends, right?
- I don't know you!


00:13:17.160 --> 00:13:18.832
- Lizards, frogs...
- Find your own hiding place!


00:13:18.960 --> 00:13:20.518
- We're practically related!
- No room at the inn!


00:13:20.640 --> 00:13:21.959
- Come on, move over!
- You're not my friend!


00:13:22.080 --> 00:13:24.071
I'll let you kiss my sister!


00:13:32.720 --> 00:13:34.278
You son of a...


00:14:26.960 --> 00:14:29.872
Where are your friends now, <i>amigo?</i>


00:14:57.280 --> 00:14:59.919
Get your slimy-webbed phalanges
off my boots!


00:15:01.000 --> 00:15:01.955
Sorry.


00:15:02.080 --> 00:15:05.152
I got a bead on you, stranger.
So you get up real slow


00:15:05.280 --> 00:15:06.633
lessen you want to spend the better part


00:15:06.760 --> 00:15:08.512
of the afternoon
putting your face back together!


00:15:08.640 --> 00:15:11.200
- No, ma'am, I don't.
- Who are you?


00:15:11.320 --> 00:15:13.515
- Who am I?
- I'm asking the questions here!


00:15:13.640 --> 00:15:15.949
Our town is drying up.
We're in the middle of a drought.


00:15:16.080 --> 00:15:17.718
Now someone's dumping water
in the desert!


00:15:17.840 --> 00:15:19.831
It's a puzzle of undeterminable size
and dimension,


00:15:19.960 --> 00:15:22.633
but I intend to find out
what role you playing in all this.


00:15:22.760 --> 00:15:25.228
- Role?
- What are you involved in?


00:15:25.600 --> 00:15:27.750
Well, I'm glad you asked.


00:15:27.880 --> 00:15:30.838
I've got two one-acts, a mystery
and a musical I've been gestating.


00:15:30.960 --> 00:15:33.918
I got the words, I'm just working on
the melody right now. It's like a...


00:15:36.040 --> 00:15:37.189
I think it's gonna be a western.


00:15:37.320 --> 00:15:39.788
<i>A monkey got a cracker</i>
<i>His mother was a slapper</i>


00:15:39.920 --> 00:15:43.356
<i>She'll be coming 'round the mountain</i>
<i>in the rain</i>


00:15:44.600 --> 00:15:47.353
You ain't from around here, are you?


00:15:48.520 --> 00:15:50.556
I'm still working on it.


00:15:52.120 --> 00:15:53.348
So, what's your name?


00:15:54.080 --> 00:15:55.877
- Beans.
- That's a funny kind of name.


00:15:56.000 --> 00:15:58.798
What can I say?
My daddy plumb loved baked beans.


00:15:58.920 --> 00:16:00.558
Well, you're lucky
he didn't plumb love asparagus.


00:16:00.680 --> 00:16:01.795
What are you saying?


00:16:01.920 --> 00:16:03.876
I mean,
I enjoy a hearty puttanesca myself,


00:16:04.000 --> 00:16:06.150
but I'm not sure that a child
would appreciate the moniker.


00:16:06.280 --> 00:16:10.671
My daddy was a great man, even if
he did exhibit a proclivity for legumes.


00:16:10.800 --> 00:16:13.189
- Spicy.
- You're eating his ashes!


00:16:14.560 --> 00:16:15.629
You carry his remains?


00:16:15.760 --> 00:16:18.877
No, his ashes. He loved to smoke.
They never found the body.


00:16:19.000 --> 00:16:20.877
Well, I'm sure he had his reasons.


00:16:21.000 --> 00:16:22.877
- What are you implying?
- Nothing.


00:16:23.000 --> 00:16:24.877
My daddy was never near
that mine shaft.


00:16:25.000 --> 00:16:26.479
He'd been sober for over a month!


00:16:26.600 --> 00:16:29.398
And for you to insinuate that he would
abandon his parental responsibilities


00:16:29.520 --> 00:16:33.274
at a delicate time in my personal
development is an affront to my sense...


00:16:36.840 --> 00:16:38.114
Miss Beans?


00:16:38.920 --> 00:16:41.229
Miss Beans? Hello?


00:16:43.160 --> 00:16:44.149
Hello?


00:16:59.800 --> 00:17:01.552
And until the people of Andromeda Five


00:17:01.680 --> 00:17:04.672
return him safe and sound,
I will not sell my ranch!


00:17:06.040 --> 00:17:08.235
- What... What are you doing?
- What are you doing?


00:17:08.360 --> 00:17:10.112
- What am I doing?
- You're cuddling me.


00:17:10.240 --> 00:17:11.559
- You were frozen.
- I was not.


00:17:11.680 --> 00:17:13.477
Yes, you were. You stopped talking.


00:17:13.600 --> 00:17:16.717
It's a defence mechanism.
Actually, lots of lizards have it.


00:17:16.840 --> 00:17:17.955
You're making that up.


00:17:18.760 --> 00:17:20.876
So, you gonna die out here,
or you want a ride into town?


00:17:21.000 --> 00:17:24.754
No, no, no. Yeah. No. Yes, please.
Thank you. Sorry.


00:17:24.880 --> 00:17:28.429
Today's Wednesday.
Wednesday's when we all get to it.


00:17:29.200 --> 00:17:30.553
So who are you, really?


00:17:30.680 --> 00:17:32.318
Well, I'm a man of many epithets.


00:17:32.440 --> 00:17:34.670
There's my stage name, my pen name,
my avatar.


00:17:34.800 --> 00:17:37.189
I had a pseudonym once,
but I had it legally changed.


00:17:37.320 --> 00:17:41.108
And so the stranger,
seeking companionship,


00:17:41.240 --> 00:17:45.358
finds the woman,
much like the sirens of ancient times


00:17:45.480 --> 00:17:49.553
luring him to his certain demise.


00:17:50.160 --> 00:17:51.832
...nom de plume, I have a CB handle.


00:17:51.960 --> 00:17:53.552
I'm actually one of the few men
with a maiden name.


00:17:53.680 --> 00:17:56.194
Whoa! Well, here we are.


00:18:03.320 --> 00:18:04.355
Right.


00:18:04.480 --> 00:18:06.914
Well, I sure do appreciate this,
Miss Beans,


00:18:07.040 --> 00:18:09.634
- and if there's ever anything that I...
- Get on up!


00:18:10.280 --> 00:18:11.679
Okay, then!


00:18:12.200 --> 00:18:14.077
See you, Beans.


00:18:30.080 --> 00:18:31.149
You heading out, Jim?


00:18:31.280 --> 00:18:34.238
Well, we gave it our best shot.
We had to sell out.


00:18:34.360 --> 00:18:37.079
Can't grow no crops without no water.


00:18:38.400 --> 00:18:40.038
Bye, now!


00:18:44.720 --> 00:18:46.039
What is it?


00:18:49.200 --> 00:18:50.189
What was that for?


00:18:50.680 --> 00:18:51.908
You're funny looking.


00:18:52.360 --> 00:18:54.555
Oh, yeah?
Well, you're funny looking, too.


00:18:54.680 --> 00:18:56.910
- That's a funny-looking shirt.
- That's a funny-looking dress.


00:18:57.040 --> 00:18:59.315
- You got funny-looking eyes!
- You got a funny-looking face!


00:19:00.360 --> 00:19:04.148
You're a stranger.
Strangers don't last long here.


00:19:04.560 --> 00:19:06.551
Here's your beans, Beans.


00:19:06.680 --> 00:19:08.591
I'm gonna need some more feed, too,
Willie.


00:19:08.720 --> 00:19:12.554
Now, Beans, you owe me three quarts
already. I can't give you more credit.


00:19:12.680 --> 00:19:14.830
But I'll have what I owe you at noon.


00:19:14.960 --> 00:19:19.954
You don't understand. It's Mr Merrimack
down at the bank. He cut off all credit.


00:19:20.080 --> 00:19:22.150
Hey, Beans! Beans!


00:19:22.360 --> 00:19:24.271
You know that there fella?


00:19:24.400 --> 00:19:25.833
Hey, Beans! Miss Beans!


00:19:26.320 --> 00:19:27.799
Nope.


00:19:27.920 --> 00:19:29.035
Hey, Beans!


00:19:29.280 --> 00:19:30.235
Hey.


00:19:31.960 --> 00:19:34.793
Right. Blend in. Yeah, blend in.


00:21:02.240 --> 00:21:03.992
I'd like a glass of water.


00:21:06.480 --> 00:21:07.515
He wants a glass of water!


00:21:07.640 --> 00:21:09.232
Make it a double!


00:21:09.360 --> 00:21:10.634
Give him the spittoon!


00:21:15.600 --> 00:21:17.875
Cactus juice. That's what we got.


00:21:41.720 --> 00:21:43.358
Hey, there, fruit cup.


00:21:43.480 --> 00:21:47.314
You're a long ways from home, ain't ya?


00:21:47.440 --> 00:21:49.795
Who exactly are you?


00:21:54.040 --> 00:21:55.234
<i>Who am I?</i>


00:21:57.000 --> 00:21:57.955
<i>I could be anyone.</i>


00:22:01.720 --> 00:22:05.713
What's the matter?
You missing your mommy's mangos?


00:22:06.800 --> 00:22:08.836
As a matter of fact, I am.


00:22:09.760 --> 00:22:11.716
But not as much as
your daddy's cooking!


00:22:13.960 --> 00:22:16.952
Exactly where did you say
you were from?


00:22:17.080 --> 00:22:20.231
Me? I'm from the West.


00:22:20.360 --> 00:22:23.432
Out there, beyond the horizon.
Past the sunset.


00:22:24.400 --> 00:22:25.958
The Far West.


00:22:27.920 --> 00:22:29.512
Yeah, that's right, <i>hombres.</i>


00:22:29.640 --> 00:22:32.234
The place I come from,
we kill a man before breakfast


00:22:32.360 --> 00:22:34.396
just to work up an appetite.


00:22:35.080 --> 00:22:37.071
Then we salt him, and we pepper him.


00:22:37.200 --> 00:22:41.159
Then we braise him in clarified butter.
And then we eat him.


00:22:41.280 --> 00:22:43.191
- You eat him?
- That's what I said!


00:22:43.320 --> 00:22:47.233
Hell, I seen things make a grown man
lose control of his glandular functions!


00:22:47.360 --> 00:22:50.397
You spend three days in a horse
carcass, living off your own juices.


00:22:50.520 --> 00:22:53.239
It'll change a man. Oh, yeah.


00:22:55.560 --> 00:22:59.917
Had a few extra aces in this deck,
gents. Just the way I like it.


00:23:00.280 --> 00:23:04.717
So, no, my hirsute little rodent friend,
I am not from around these parts.


00:23:04.840 --> 00:23:07.035
You might say I'm from everywhere
there's trouble brewing


00:23:07.160 --> 00:23:09.310
and hell waiting to be raised.


00:23:09.440 --> 00:23:12.671
You might say
I'm what hell's already raised up.


00:23:13.920 --> 00:23:15.399
Name's


00:23:16.160 --> 00:23:17.673
Rango.


00:23:19.080 --> 00:23:20.195
Rango.


00:23:21.920 --> 00:23:23.911
Are you the fella
that killed them Jenkins brothers?


00:23:25.080 --> 00:23:27.230
Killed them with one bullet.


00:23:27.360 --> 00:23:29.032
Don't get no deader.


00:23:29.160 --> 00:23:31.071
All seven of them?


00:23:32.160 --> 00:23:33.513
That's right.


00:23:34.080 --> 00:23:35.752
All seven of them.


00:23:36.640 --> 00:23:39.791
Exactly how you do that, Mr Rango?


00:23:42.280 --> 00:23:43.998
You know, I'm glad you asked me that.


00:23:44.120 --> 00:23:47.874
And I will be happy to tell you how.
But you're all gonna have to listen up!


00:23:49.120 --> 00:23:51.236
Because this is where it gets


00:23:52.000 --> 00:23:53.558
complicated.


00:23:55.600 --> 00:23:58.353
That'll close out your account,
Mrs Oats, two gulps and a swig.


00:23:58.480 --> 00:24:01.756
Hands off, Mordecai! That's what's left
of your college education!


00:24:03.920 --> 00:24:06.070
I don't rightly have
no other choice, Beans.


00:24:06.200 --> 00:24:10.113
Times being so hard,
we just can't give no more credit.


00:24:10.760 --> 00:24:13.320
But this here is a bank.
This is where you keep the water.


00:24:16.400 --> 00:24:20.518
Beans, you've been like a niece to me
ever since your daddy


00:24:22.000 --> 00:24:25.390
did not fall drunk down a mine shaft.


00:24:25.520 --> 00:24:29.832
I've tried to protect you and others
from certain realities.


00:24:29.960 --> 00:24:31.837
But that... Well...


00:24:32.400 --> 00:24:34.038
- Mr Merrimack?
- Realities are bearing down.


00:24:34.160 --> 00:24:35.593
Mr Merrimack!


00:24:36.440 --> 00:24:37.555
Are you all right?


00:24:38.200 --> 00:24:41.510
Beans, I need to show you something.


00:24:48.960 --> 00:24:52.236
- That's all that's left?
- And this here is the reserve!


00:24:52.360 --> 00:24:53.918
I don't know if you've noticed,


00:24:54.040 --> 00:24:57.350
but folks just ain't making deposits
on a Wednesday no more!


00:24:57.480 --> 00:25:00.756
Mr Merrimack, if I don't get some water,
I'm gonna lose my ranch


00:25:00.880 --> 00:25:03.110
and you're telling me
that's all that's left in the whole town?


00:25:03.240 --> 00:25:06.232
Now that just don't make no sense.
Now, listen.


00:25:06.360 --> 00:25:10.148
Someone is dumping water
in the desert.


00:25:10.840 --> 00:25:13.434
I seen it with my own eyes.


00:25:15.200 --> 00:25:16.997
Water in the desert?


00:25:17.120 --> 00:25:19.998
Was this during
one of your special times?


00:25:20.320 --> 00:25:21.275
No.


00:25:21.400 --> 00:25:25.279
Well, we can all dream,
but this is the reality.


00:25:25.400 --> 00:25:28.836
Why do you think so many people
are selling out? They just can't make it.


00:25:28.960 --> 00:25:31.269
Well, what am I supposed to do?


00:25:31.720 --> 00:25:34.280
Well, I suppose
we could talk to the Mayor.


00:25:34.400 --> 00:25:37.392
I hear he's been helping people out
in this time of crisis.


00:25:37.520 --> 00:25:38.555
The Mayor?


00:25:38.680 --> 00:25:41.240
He may be our only hope.


00:25:41.360 --> 00:25:44.158
Bullet hits a shovel, ricochets back
towards number three,


00:25:44.280 --> 00:25:45.554
and that's when the roof caved in,


00:25:45.680 --> 00:25:47.671
igniting the thermos
of pure grain alcohol


00:25:47.800 --> 00:25:51.429
instantly vapourising his bodily form,
leaving nothing but a charcoal statue


00:25:51.560 --> 00:25:53.551
and a high-pitched squeal.


00:25:59.120 --> 00:26:02.874
Hold on, there. That's only six.
What happened to number seven?


00:26:04.120 --> 00:26:05.348
Number seven?


00:26:05.480 --> 00:26:07.675
Hell, he died of infection.


00:26:10.840 --> 00:26:12.751
- Seven men!
- One bullet!


00:26:12.880 --> 00:26:14.757
Drinks all around!


00:26:17.520 --> 00:26:19.476
Dance for me, Sod Buster!


00:26:19.600 --> 00:26:22.194
- Yes, dance like a chicken!
- That's right! Dance!


00:26:23.640 --> 00:26:25.676
You got corn in your ears, mate?


00:26:25.800 --> 00:26:28.598
You don't pay the mortgage,
you don't own the land!


00:26:28.720 --> 00:26:31.632
- That's basic real estate law, my friend.
- Quid pro quo!


00:26:31.760 --> 00:26:34.672
If I see your face in this town again,


00:26:34.800 --> 00:26:38.998
I'm gonna slice it off and use it
to wipe my unmentionables.


00:26:39.680 --> 00:26:40.795
Mind the beak.


00:26:41.960 --> 00:26:44.394
And don't come back!


00:26:46.160 --> 00:26:48.754
What are you all gawping at?


00:26:52.200 --> 00:26:55.556
Hey, Bad Bill,
there's something I got to tell you!


00:27:00.040 --> 00:27:01.234
What is this?


00:27:01.360 --> 00:27:05.194
You know who that is, Bill?
That there's Rango!


00:27:05.320 --> 00:27:08.949
Yeah, he ain't afraid of you!
He ain't afraid of none of you.


00:27:09.080 --> 00:27:10.433
Killed them Jenkins brothers.


00:27:10.560 --> 00:27:13.313
- Done it with one bullet, Bill.
- All seven of them!


00:27:14.000 --> 00:27:15.797
Is that right?


00:27:52.000 --> 00:27:54.116
Let me get that before you...


00:27:58.440 --> 00:28:00.078
No. Oh, I know. Here.


00:28:03.800 --> 00:28:06.189
Just take care of that for you.


00:28:07.000 --> 00:28:09.070
There. All better.


00:28:32.520 --> 00:28:34.954
T.O. T.O. Just a second.


00:28:37.200 --> 00:28:38.519
All right, now listen!


00:28:38.640 --> 00:28:41.712
I'm going to give you fellas
one last chance to reconsider!


00:28:46.080 --> 00:28:49.152
And if you don't want to reconsider


00:28:49.280 --> 00:28:52.192
I might consider reconsidering myself.


00:29:03.120 --> 00:29:06.351
Now that's what I'm talking about. Yeah.


00:29:06.480 --> 00:29:07.993
All right, now listen up!


00:29:08.120 --> 00:29:10.998
Things are going to be different
around here now that Rango's in town.


00:29:11.120 --> 00:29:14.032
Got some new rules!
I want my shoes shined every morning,


00:29:14.160 --> 00:29:15.957
my coffee hot, Danish on the side.


00:29:16.080 --> 00:29:18.196
Whatever you do,
don't look me in the eye.


00:29:18.320 --> 00:29:20.629
Stay out of my peripheral vision!


00:29:20.960 --> 00:29:22.632
- It's Rango.
- What's he up to?


00:29:22.760 --> 00:29:25.752
He ain't afraid of nobody.
He's telling that bird what's for!


00:29:25.880 --> 00:29:27.552
And when you see me coming,
stand aside.


00:29:27.880 --> 00:29:30.519
I take large steps and I don't want
none of you hayseeds


00:29:30.640 --> 00:29:33.200
getting your bodily fluids on my boots!


00:29:34.600 --> 00:29:37.672
Of course, there is no need for violence,


00:29:37.800 --> 00:29:40.598
as long as we stick together,
work as a team.


00:29:40.720 --> 00:29:43.951
So I want you all to come outside now
and line up single file


00:29:44.080 --> 00:29:45.433
while I take a brief intermission!


00:29:48.240 --> 00:29:49.958
What's he doing now?


00:29:50.080 --> 00:29:51.559
I think it's a number two.


00:30:12.280 --> 00:30:14.111
Never mind.


00:30:34.240 --> 00:30:35.832
Take a look-see over here!


00:30:35.960 --> 00:30:37.109
Well, look at him now!


00:30:37.240 --> 00:30:38.992
He's chasing after that hawk!


00:30:39.120 --> 00:30:40.519
Give him hell, Rango!


00:32:28.560 --> 00:32:31.233
- Did you see that?
- He killed that thing!


00:32:31.360 --> 00:32:32.873
What do you think, Doc?


00:32:33.640 --> 00:32:36.200
This hawk is dead!


00:32:36.840 --> 00:32:39.149
Shoot, I say we cook that right up.


00:32:39.280 --> 00:32:40.872
He did it with one bullet!


00:32:41.000 --> 00:32:42.433
Just like he said!


00:32:42.560 --> 00:32:44.198
It's about time
we had a hero around here.


00:32:44.320 --> 00:32:46.436
One who ain't in a pine box.


00:32:47.120 --> 00:32:49.839
I think it's time he met the Mayor.


00:32:49.960 --> 00:32:52.758
You hear that, Rango?
You're going to meet the Mayor!


00:32:52.880 --> 00:32:55.075
Let's hear it for Rango!


00:32:58.320 --> 00:33:00.629
And so the stranger basks


00:33:00.760 --> 00:33:03.957
in the adulation of his new friends,


00:33:04.080 --> 00:33:09.029
sinking deeper into the guacamole
of his own deception.


00:33:09.160 --> 00:33:10.718
When is he going to die?


00:33:10.840 --> 00:33:13.149
Soon, <i>compadre.</i> Soon.


00:33:29.080 --> 00:33:30.957
My land is not for sale!


00:33:32.120 --> 00:33:34.509
I came here to save my land, not sell it!


00:33:34.640 --> 00:33:38.110
I'm sure there's something reasonable
we can work out if you just talk to him!


00:33:39.480 --> 00:33:41.152
Beans! Where are you going? Beans?


00:33:41.720 --> 00:33:43.438
The Mayor will see you now.


00:33:48.720 --> 00:33:51.837
Water, Mr Rango, water.


00:33:52.320 --> 00:33:55.471
Without it,
there's nothing but dust and decay.


00:33:55.600 --> 00:33:59.878
But with water there's life.


00:34:04.760 --> 00:34:06.830
Look at them, so desperate to live,
they'll follow it anywhere.


00:34:07.480 --> 00:34:09.516
That's the immutable law of the desert.


00:34:11.360 --> 00:34:15.353
Control the water
and you control everything.


00:34:15.480 --> 00:34:17.550
This is from my private stock.


00:34:17.680 --> 00:34:20.638
Vintage rainwater
from the Great Deluge.


00:34:21.720 --> 00:34:23.836
Not Noah's deluge.
Good heavens, I'm not that old.


00:34:27.360 --> 00:34:29.635
I guess power has its privileges.


00:34:30.200 --> 00:34:31.599
You make a good point, son.


00:34:32.760 --> 00:34:35.558
But with privilege comes responsibility.


00:34:37.160 --> 00:34:39.958
Hell, I was mayor here
before there was a Dirt!


00:34:40.080 --> 00:34:43.231
And I may be
just a sentimental old turtle


00:34:43.360 --> 00:34:48.115
but I think there's a future for this town.
And I hope you'll be part of it.


00:34:50.200 --> 00:34:52.555
- To Dirt!
- To Dirt.


00:34:55.560 --> 00:34:58.836
You see them, Mr Rango?
All my friends and neighbours?


00:34:59.840 --> 00:35:02.991
It's a hard life here. Very hard.


00:35:03.960 --> 00:35:07.350
Do you know how they make it through
each and every day?


00:35:07.480 --> 00:35:08.435
They believe.


00:35:09.080 --> 00:35:11.833
They believe it's going to be better.


00:35:11.960 --> 00:35:15.157
They believe that the water will come.


00:35:15.280 --> 00:35:17.635
They believe against all odds
and all evidence


00:35:17.760 --> 00:35:19.830
that tomorrow will be better than today.


00:35:22.000 --> 00:35:23.433
People have to believe in something.


00:35:25.440 --> 00:35:28.352
Right now, they believe in you.


00:35:30.520 --> 00:35:34.559
Pick it up, Mr Rango.
Your destiny awaits.


00:35:37.920 --> 00:35:41.196
People have to believe in something.


00:35:45.240 --> 00:35:46.195
It just don't make no sense.


00:35:47.960 --> 00:35:48.631
This whole town is drying up,


00:35:48.760 --> 00:35:51.228
and the Mayor is the only one
who don't seem to be affected.


00:35:51.360 --> 00:35:53.237
Doesn't that make you
just a wee bit suspicious?


00:35:53.400 --> 00:35:56.392
And what about that water
I saw out in the desert?


00:35:56.520 --> 00:36:00.672
All right! No need to incite anxiety.
I'll inquire about the Mayor.


00:36:00.800 --> 00:36:04.315
But if you really feel
there's some conspiracy occurring,


00:36:04.440 --> 00:36:07.318
I suggest you take it up
with the new sheriff.


00:36:08.640 --> 00:36:11.518
This is going to be good. Hey!
Watch that needle there.


00:36:11.640 --> 00:36:12.993
Not too tight.
I want to leave room for some pucker!


00:36:13.120 --> 00:36:14.075
That's good.


00:36:14.200 --> 00:36:15.155
Oh, easy there, tiger.


00:36:16.920 --> 00:36:17.909
- A little up and back?
- I don't think so.


00:36:18.040 --> 00:36:19.109
Have you got French cuffs with that?


00:36:19.240 --> 00:36:20.468
Excuse me, Sheriff Rango.
I want to talk to you.


00:36:20.600 --> 00:36:21.999
Hey, Beans,
what do you think of the new duds?


00:36:22.120 --> 00:36:23.997
I got a 10-gallon hat
marked down from 15.


00:36:24.120 --> 00:36:25.599
- That's nice.
- Have you met Angelique?


00:36:25.720 --> 00:36:27.438
- Hello, Beans.
- Hello, Angelique.


00:36:27.560 --> 00:36:28.515
- Tart.
- Floozy.


00:36:28.640 --> 00:36:30.710
- Trollop.
- Excuse me, Mr Rango.


00:36:30.840 --> 00:36:32.353
I will blow that ugly right off your face!


00:36:32.680 --> 00:36:34.557
I was just thinking that...


00:36:35.320 --> 00:36:36.912
You want the old John Hancock,
do you?


00:36:37.040 --> 00:36:39.031
- Well, here. Hold this.
- Sheriff Rango, this isn't a social call.


00:36:39.160 --> 00:36:40.752
There's a bullet in there.


00:36:40.880 --> 00:36:42.313
I know about the shindig this afternoon.


00:36:42.440 --> 00:36:44.795
- I ordered myself some right fancy duds.
- Sheriff, I'd like to file a...


00:36:44.920 --> 00:36:46.558
- Mr Rango!
- Oh, you, too? No problem.


00:36:46.680 --> 00:36:48.193
- Here, let me just...
- I need you to investigate...


00:36:48.320 --> 00:36:51.039
You know, Beans, I bet you clean up
real nice, you put a little effort into it.


00:36:51.160 --> 00:36:52.275
- What?
- Now, remember, son,


00:36:52.400 --> 00:36:54.789
stay in school, eat your veggies,
burn everything but Shakespeare.


00:36:54.920 --> 00:36:56.433
- Who's Shakespeare?
- Sheriff Rango,


00:36:56.920 --> 00:36:58.558
if that is your real name.


00:36:58.680 --> 00:37:00.750
I am trying to save my daddy's ranch,


00:37:00.880 --> 00:37:02.836
which is on the verge
of an agricultural meltdown


00:37:02.960 --> 00:37:05.713
while you're playing patty-cake
with this here trollop!


00:37:07.880 --> 00:37:11.031
Sad, really. Such a drab little thing.


00:37:11.720 --> 00:37:12.789
Why does she do that?


00:37:12.920 --> 00:37:15.992
- It's a survival reflex.
- Her switch is just broken.


00:37:16.120 --> 00:37:17.473
Well, that's an inconvenience.


00:37:17.600 --> 00:37:20.068
It is not a rash! It is a birthmark!


00:37:21.720 --> 00:37:22.914
I did it again, didn't I?


00:37:23.040 --> 00:37:24.189
Did what?


00:37:24.600 --> 00:37:26.079
Let me ask you something.


00:37:26.200 --> 00:37:30.079
Did anybody here mention
what happened to our last sheriff?


00:38:07.840 --> 00:38:11.992
Pardon, but may I ask you...
Excuse me, may I ask you...


00:38:12.120 --> 00:38:15.749
The last sheriff... Pardon me.
Where is everybody going?


00:38:16.320 --> 00:38:19.118
What exactly happened to the...


00:38:23.320 --> 00:38:24.799
<i>All day</i>


00:38:24.920 --> 00:38:28.708
<i>I've faced the barren waste</i>


00:38:29.240 --> 00:38:32.915
<i>Without the taste of water</i>


00:38:36.680 --> 00:38:39.990
<i>Cool water</i>


00:38:43.320 --> 00:38:46.312
<i>Old Dan and I</i>


00:38:46.440 --> 00:38:48.317
<i>With throats burned dry</i>


00:38:48.880 --> 00:38:52.873
<i>And souls that cry</i>


00:38:53.000 --> 00:38:55.434
<i>For water</i>


00:38:56.160 --> 00:38:57.912
I'm so sorry. I'm so sorry.


00:38:58.480 --> 00:39:00.311
<i>Cool</i>


00:39:00.920 --> 00:39:04.549
<i>Clear water</i>


00:39:07.800 --> 00:39:09.438
This is a heck of a hoedown
you got going.


00:39:09.560 --> 00:39:11.232
Still working out those steps.


00:39:11.360 --> 00:39:15.035
So, is this considered
normal civic behaviour?


00:39:15.160 --> 00:39:17.515
Every Wednesday, just like clockwork.


00:39:17.640 --> 00:39:19.278
You kill bird.


00:39:19.440 --> 00:39:22.113
Yeah. Matter of fact, I did.


00:39:22.240 --> 00:39:23.434
Bird dead. Snake come.


00:39:25.360 --> 00:39:26.315
Snake?


00:39:26.440 --> 00:39:27.395
He means Rattlesnake Jake, Mr Rango.


00:39:27.520 --> 00:39:29.556
He never comes to town 'cause
he's scared of that hawk.


00:39:29.680 --> 00:39:30.874
But he might come now.


00:39:31.000 --> 00:39:32.479
Can I have your boots
when you're dead?


00:39:32.600 --> 00:39:33.589
No!


00:39:33.720 --> 00:39:35.950
And I ain't got no problem
with this Rattlesnake Jake.


00:39:36.080 --> 00:39:37.638
That's just what Amos said.


00:39:37.920 --> 00:39:39.751
Amos?


00:39:43.000 --> 00:39:45.195
You got any gold fillings?


00:40:02.760 --> 00:40:05.194
<i>My fellow Dirtonians.</i>


00:40:05.320 --> 00:40:10.075
<i>I welcome you to our great day</i>
<i>of deliverance. Hallelujah.</i>


00:40:10.200 --> 00:40:11.679
- Hallelujah!
- Hallelujah!


00:40:11.800 --> 00:40:15.156
<i>Acolytes, prepare the holy spigot!</i>


00:40:25.360 --> 00:40:28.511
<i>We have a newcomer</i>
<i>amongst us today, my friends.</i>


00:40:28.640 --> 00:40:31.234
<i>A man I think needs</i>
<i>little introduction to you</i>


00:40:31.360 --> 00:40:35.319
<i>so bold has been his entry</i>
<i>into our fair society.</i>


00:40:35.440 --> 00:40:38.512
<i>Mr Rango, would you step forward?</i>


00:40:44.160 --> 00:40:48.278
<i>The time has come, my friends.</i>
<i>The time that was foretold!</i>


00:40:48.400 --> 00:40:49.958
- Hallelujah!
- Hallelujah!


00:40:50.080 --> 00:40:51.399
<i>The sacred time!</i>


00:40:51.520 --> 00:40:53.192
- Hallelujah!
- Hallelujah!


00:40:53.320 --> 00:40:55.550
<i>The time of destiny!</i>


00:40:55.680 --> 00:40:57.159
- Hallelujah!
- Hallelujah!


00:40:57.280 --> 00:40:59.635
<i>The time of deliverance!</i>


00:40:59.760 --> 00:41:00.715
- Hallelujah!
- Hallelujah!


00:41:00.840 --> 00:41:04.753
<i>It is the time of hydration!</i>


00:41:19.680 --> 00:41:21.955
- It's his fault!
- It's the newcomer!


00:41:22.080 --> 00:41:23.672
- Burn him!
- He's a witch!


00:41:23.800 --> 00:41:24.835
I get his boots!


00:41:24.960 --> 00:41:28.999
<i>My friends, my friends!</i>
<i>Temper your frustrations.</i>


00:41:29.120 --> 00:41:33.955
<i>Times will be tough from now on.</i>
<i>Sacrifices will have to be made.</i>


00:41:34.080 --> 00:41:37.550
<i>But if I can help in any way,</i>
<i>please know that my door is always...</i>


00:41:37.680 --> 00:41:39.193
Hold it, hold it!


00:41:39.320 --> 00:41:41.959
Now, this whole thing
stinks three ways to Sunday.


00:41:42.080 --> 00:41:44.435
First the bank's run dry
and now this here spigot?


00:41:44.560 --> 00:41:45.515
The bank's run dry?


00:41:45.640 --> 00:41:48.200
- What's she talking about?
- She said there's no water in the bank!


00:41:53.280 --> 00:41:56.272
This is all we have!
We can't give it all out!


00:41:56.400 --> 00:41:58.470
That was my rehydration account!


00:41:59.880 --> 00:42:03.668
None of that civil disobedience
in my town, thank you very much.


00:42:06.200 --> 00:42:09.317
Thank goodness you're here, Sheriff.
Things were getting out of hand.


00:42:09.440 --> 00:42:11.192
Come right in.


00:42:11.320 --> 00:42:15.154
Let me have a gander at the source
of the societal discontentment here.


00:42:17.880 --> 00:42:19.199
Mercy.


00:42:19.320 --> 00:42:21.880
All right, listen up! I've been thinking


00:42:22.000 --> 00:42:24.639
and I believe I've figured something out.


00:42:24.760 --> 00:42:27.069
You folks have a water problem!


00:42:29.040 --> 00:42:31.508
Now just pay attention, everybody.
I'm trying to make a point here.


00:42:31.640 --> 00:42:34.279
Let's say this fella here
were to take a drink of water.


00:42:34.400 --> 00:42:37.039
Just one little drink.
No harm, no foul, right?


00:42:40.120 --> 00:42:41.189
And you!


00:42:41.560 --> 00:42:44.154
You're just as dried up and parched
as a jackrabbit in July.


00:42:44.280 --> 00:42:47.192
So you belly on up
and take you a double shot!


00:42:48.400 --> 00:42:50.152
Stay with me.


00:42:51.040 --> 00:42:54.715
What do you think happens then?
Why we'd all be drinking!


00:42:55.440 --> 00:42:58.193
And before you know it,
there wouldn't be any more water.


00:42:58.320 --> 00:43:00.197
And then where would we be?


00:43:01.520 --> 00:43:03.158
We'd be thirsty.


00:43:03.720 --> 00:43:05.312
Real thirsty.


00:43:05.760 --> 00:43:08.115
We'd turn on each other
like a bunch of animals!


00:43:10.680 --> 00:43:15.310
Now look here.
We have got six days of water.


00:43:20.160 --> 00:43:22.720
We have got five days...


00:43:24.080 --> 00:43:27.629
As long as we've got water,
we've got ourselves a town.


00:43:28.840 --> 00:43:30.637
Sheriff Rango is right.


00:43:30.760 --> 00:43:34.196
As long as we have this water,
we have some hope.


00:43:34.320 --> 00:43:35.992
And you can all take it from me.


00:43:36.120 --> 00:43:39.396
My 100% full-time employment
from this moment on


00:43:39.520 --> 00:43:43.274
will be to protect
our precious natural resource.


00:43:43.400 --> 00:43:47.029
Ain't no one gonna tango
with the Rango.


00:43:59.440 --> 00:44:00.589
Evening, ladies.


00:44:00.720 --> 00:44:02.392
Evening, Sheriff.


00:44:02.520 --> 00:44:04.511
And don't you come back!


00:44:04.640 --> 00:44:08.030
Hold on there, Gordy. You get back
in there and you assert yourself,


00:44:08.160 --> 00:44:11.232
and I think you'll find the people of this
here town to be surprisingly hospitable.


00:44:11.360 --> 00:44:12.554
Thank you, Sheriff.


00:44:12.680 --> 00:44:14.432
What? Not you again!


00:44:15.880 --> 00:44:17.552
I stand corrected.


00:44:23.440 --> 00:44:25.829
- This ain't the bank.
- I told you, Jedidiah!


00:44:25.960 --> 00:44:27.154
Hold it right there!


00:44:27.280 --> 00:44:28.474
- Who's that?
- It's the Sheriff!


00:44:28.600 --> 00:44:30.158
Get them hands up
where I can see them!


00:44:30.880 --> 00:44:32.836
Just as I suspected.


00:44:32.960 --> 00:44:35.554
Prospecting without the authorised
equipment. Don't move a muscle.


00:44:36.360 --> 00:44:37.759
Prospecting?


00:44:41.720 --> 00:44:44.314
Now, you got your shovel,
pickaxe, Benadryl, loofah,


00:44:44.440 --> 00:44:47.512
assorted snacks, some puzzle books
and you're gonna need a permit.


00:44:47.640 --> 00:44:49.232
- Loofah.
- Ezekiel, Jedidiah!


00:44:49.360 --> 00:44:51.476
What the Sam Hill's going on up there?


00:44:51.600 --> 00:44:54.990
I've had polyps removed
smarter than the two of you!


00:44:55.480 --> 00:44:57.550
Hell's fire, this ain't the bank!


00:44:57.720 --> 00:45:01.110
Pappy, the Sheriff is standing right here,
helping us out.


00:45:01.240 --> 00:45:03.834
Gonna give us a permit for prospecting.


00:45:03.960 --> 00:45:06.394
That's right, sir. Just doing my duty.


00:45:07.160 --> 00:45:09.116
The lonely constable on his rounds,


00:45:09.240 --> 00:45:11.435
keeping an eagle eye out
for mayhem and malfeasance.


00:45:12.000 --> 00:45:13.877
Does he look like he sounds?


00:45:15.320 --> 00:45:18.915
Well, Sheriff,
if we was to hit the mother lode,


00:45:19.040 --> 00:45:21.031
being prospectors and such,


00:45:21.160 --> 00:45:24.152
where would we deposit said annuity?


00:45:24.280 --> 00:45:26.111
Here in the town of Dirt,
we happen to have


00:45:26.240 --> 00:45:28.913
the finest financial institution
this side of the Missouri.


00:45:30.640 --> 00:45:33.074
Protected morning, noon and night
by yours truly.


00:45:34.800 --> 00:45:36.677
Much obliged.


00:45:36.920 --> 00:45:39.639
The bank's been robbed!
The bank's been robbed!


00:45:39.760 --> 00:45:42.069
Good Lord, the bank's been robbed!


00:45:42.200 --> 00:45:43.519
What's going on?


00:45:43.640 --> 00:45:45.710
- It's gone! The water's all gone!
- What'd he say?


00:45:45.840 --> 00:45:47.034
He said the bank's been robbed!


00:45:47.960 --> 00:45:50.633
Dr Marx! I'm on fire! Embrace me!


00:45:51.280 --> 00:45:55.671
<i>The bank's been robbed, the town is dry</i>
<i>"We'll die of thirst," the people cry</i>


00:45:55.800 --> 00:46:00.112
<i>He promised to protect the vault</i>
<i>The water's gone, it's all his fault</i>


00:46:00.800 --> 00:46:02.631
All right, folks, stand back,
clear the area.


00:46:02.760 --> 00:46:03.988
This is a crime scene now.


00:46:04.120 --> 00:46:07.078
Secure the perimeter, dust for prints,
check for fibres, scan for DNA.


00:46:07.200 --> 00:46:09.760
I want a urine sample from everyone.
And get me a latte.


00:46:09.880 --> 00:46:11.115
And don't mix up the two.


00:46:11.240 --> 00:46:12.309
What's this?


00:46:12.440 --> 00:46:13.998
"Prospecting Permit."


00:46:14.120 --> 00:46:15.792
I'll take that. Material evidence.


00:46:15.920 --> 00:46:17.353
What are we gonna do now, Sheriff?


00:46:17.480 --> 00:46:20.040
- We need that water.
- We're all going to die!


00:46:20.160 --> 00:46:23.596
My friends, we all know
what we have to do now.


00:46:23.720 --> 00:46:27.315
That's right.
We all know what we have to do now.


00:46:27.440 --> 00:46:29.351
- And that would be?
- Form a posse.


00:46:29.480 --> 00:46:31.232
Form a possum!


00:46:33.440 --> 00:46:34.998
A posse.


00:46:36.240 --> 00:46:39.152
Now, we're gonna be doing this
in an orderly fashion.


00:46:39.760 --> 00:46:44.436
First off, does anybody here know
how to use a firearm of any kind?


00:46:46.840 --> 00:46:48.353
All right, then.


00:46:48.480 --> 00:46:49.913
What do we do now, Sheriff?


00:46:50.040 --> 00:46:52.600
Now we ride!


00:47:05.080 --> 00:47:07.355
Where are we going?


00:47:07.480 --> 00:47:08.629
What?


00:47:08.760 --> 00:47:10.478
Where are we going?


00:47:18.440 --> 00:47:21.193
Now, as my deputy, you'll be in charge
of all tracking and finding of villains,


00:47:21.320 --> 00:47:23.993
utilising your well-developed
Injun-uity, no offence taken.


00:47:24.120 --> 00:47:25.269
So which way do you think they went?


00:47:25.400 --> 00:47:27.834
You want to sniff the air or commune
with a buffalo or something?


00:47:31.440 --> 00:47:33.192
Oh, you're good.


00:47:35.720 --> 00:47:37.312
I'm depending on you, Spoons.


00:47:37.440 --> 00:47:39.954
You got a little tobaccy
in the beard there.


00:47:40.080 --> 00:47:42.878
Always good to have a medical man
along, Doc.


00:47:43.000 --> 00:47:45.594
Reptiles got to stick together, right,
my brother?


00:47:45.720 --> 00:47:46.914
I'm an amphibian.


00:47:47.040 --> 00:47:48.473
Ain't no shame in that.


00:47:51.640 --> 00:47:53.995
You sure you're
fit for duty there, soldier?


00:47:55.840 --> 00:47:57.558
Well, you got a little something
in your eye there.


00:47:58.320 --> 00:48:01.915
Oh, that? That there's conjunctivitis, sir.
It's hereditary.


00:48:02.920 --> 00:48:05.673
Well, I'm glad to hear
it's not contagious.


00:48:06.360 --> 00:48:09.830
Now, just wait a cotton-picking minute!
A posse ain't no place for a...


00:48:10.600 --> 00:48:11.828
Never mind.


00:48:11.960 --> 00:48:13.791
Hold on there, little sister.


00:48:13.920 --> 00:48:16.480
Someone's gonna have
to look after the town while I'm gone.


00:48:18.280 --> 00:48:19.599
Can I gut-shoot someone?


00:48:20.920 --> 00:48:22.831
Let's put a pin in that.


00:48:23.360 --> 00:48:26.158
Sheriff, you're going to bring
that water back, aren't you?


00:48:27.040 --> 00:48:28.439
Count on it, little sister.


00:48:31.760 --> 00:48:34.797
- Which way do we go, Sheriff?
- There's tunnels everywhere.


00:48:34.920 --> 00:48:36.592
Whole town's perforated with them.


00:48:36.720 --> 00:48:39.473
How'd them fellers
find the bank, anyway?


00:48:39.600 --> 00:48:41.591
Gentlemen, if we can just
stay on task here.


00:48:41.720 --> 00:48:44.109
Sheriff! Over here!


00:48:49.480 --> 00:48:50.356
- Would you look at that?
- Like seeing the face of God.


00:48:50.480 --> 00:48:51.629
Amen, brother.


00:48:51.760 --> 00:48:54.194
I remember when it used to flow
every Wednesday.


00:48:54.320 --> 00:48:56.197
Those were the halcyon days.


00:48:56.320 --> 00:48:57.469
Must be a reason she quit on us.


00:48:59.120 --> 00:49:02.556
Whatever the reason,
something is controlling this here water.


00:49:02.680 --> 00:49:03.795
What do you say, Sheriff?


00:49:05.240 --> 00:49:08.073
Clearly, the robbers came
from this direction.


00:49:08.200 --> 00:49:10.475
I say we track this pipe
back to its hydraulic origin


00:49:10.600 --> 00:49:12.955
and apprehend the culprits
behind this aquatic conundrum.


00:49:13.080 --> 00:49:15.275
- What'd he say?
- I think he said follow the pipe.


00:49:15.400 --> 00:49:16.549
- He said follow the pipe.
- He said follow the pipe.


00:49:28.280 --> 00:49:32.398
Whatever you do, do not look down.


00:49:34.840 --> 00:49:37.798
- What is this place?
- It's an aquifer.


00:49:39.640 --> 00:49:41.039
What's an aquifer?


00:49:41.160 --> 00:49:43.037
Well, it's for aqua.


00:49:44.040 --> 00:49:45.792
Well, it's empty now.


00:50:03.760 --> 00:50:04.715
That's a big one.


00:50:08.680 --> 00:50:11.274
- It's the end of the line.
- Don't go no further.


00:50:11.400 --> 00:50:14.870
Someone or something
is messing with our hydration


00:50:15.000 --> 00:50:16.831
and that pipe
has got something to do with it.


00:50:16.960 --> 00:50:18.678
I thought
we was following bank robbers!


00:50:18.800 --> 00:50:20.950
We're experiencing a paradigm shift.


00:50:21.080 --> 00:50:23.036
I'm gonna shift the features on your face
if you don't shut up!


00:50:23.160 --> 00:50:24.115
Go ahead and try!


00:50:26.400 --> 00:50:29.039
Quiet, you savages! Stop your rattling.
You're affecting my cogitation.


00:50:31.360 --> 00:50:34.193
Whoa! I got it. Snuff out them torches.


00:50:39.760 --> 00:50:40.715
Sure enough.


00:50:41.320 --> 00:50:42.958
Smart thinking there, feller.


00:50:43.080 --> 00:50:45.640
- Start climbing.
- Get your foot out of my face!


00:50:45.760 --> 00:50:47.193
Not bad, huh, Beans?


00:50:47.320 --> 00:50:49.595
You keep thinking like that,
your hat's gonna catch on fire.


00:50:49.720 --> 00:50:52.029
Well, you know, you get on a roll,
you just...


00:50:52.880 --> 00:50:54.108
Hot, hot! Burn.


00:51:05.080 --> 00:51:08.277
Poor things.
All they wanted was a little water.


00:51:08.400 --> 00:51:11.676
Cactus dying of thirst. It don't bode well.


00:51:11.800 --> 00:51:13.392
- Hey, look what I found!
- What you got there?


00:51:13.520 --> 00:51:16.273
- I saw that first!
- Hey, that's mine!


00:51:16.400 --> 00:51:17.879
Give me that!


00:51:18.000 --> 00:51:19.877
It's empty anyway.


00:51:20.000 --> 00:51:21.353
I knew that.


00:51:21.480 --> 00:51:22.674
Where'd you find that?


00:51:22.800 --> 00:51:25.473
Sheriff! You're going to want to see this!


00:51:29.040 --> 00:51:30.632
It's Mr Merrimack from the bank.


00:51:30.760 --> 00:51:32.079
What's he doing here?


00:51:32.200 --> 00:51:33.633
- Everybody stand back.
- All right, let me see.


00:51:33.760 --> 00:51:36.115
Looks like them varmints shot him
in the back.


00:51:36.240 --> 00:51:40.199
No, this man wasn't shot.
He was drowned!


00:51:40.320 --> 00:51:42.834
- Drowned?
- In the middle of the desert?


00:51:42.960 --> 00:51:44.598
What a way to go.


00:51:46.240 --> 00:51:49.789
Well, now, whose boot prints are those?


00:51:53.520 --> 00:51:55.795
That's interesting.
The ground's still wet.


00:51:57.440 --> 00:51:59.112
I suppose we should bury him.


00:51:59.240 --> 00:52:02.676
- I don't know. Birds got to eat, too.
- Circle of life!


00:52:03.760 --> 00:52:06.433
Hey! What's that dad-gum Indian doing?


00:52:10.640 --> 00:52:13.200
I see you're consulting with the spirits.


00:52:13.320 --> 00:52:15.276
No, I'm moulting.
Means I'm ready to mate.


00:52:17.640 --> 00:52:19.073
I'll keep that in mind.


00:52:19.760 --> 00:52:20.795
Cactus fruit.


00:52:20.920 --> 00:52:23.559
Ah, yes. The ancient cactus fruit.


00:52:23.680 --> 00:52:25.352
I believe your people use it
as seasoning


00:52:25.480 --> 00:52:26.833
when preparing your native dishes.


00:52:26.960 --> 00:52:28.678
Also natural laxative.


00:52:30.320 --> 00:52:31.309
Pick up trail.


00:52:31.440 --> 00:52:34.716
Three men heading west.
One blind, one with


00:52:36.320 --> 00:52:38.595
enlarged prostate, riding sidesaddle.


00:52:38.720 --> 00:52:41.837
- What did he say?
- They're riding sidesaddle.


00:52:41.960 --> 00:52:43.279
- We're whispering.
- What'd he say?


00:52:43.400 --> 00:52:44.435
Someone's got a bad valve.


00:52:44.560 --> 00:52:47.358
All right, which one of you fellers
needs a check-up?


00:52:48.320 --> 00:52:49.355
Awkward.


00:52:50.680 --> 00:52:53.797
What exactly are we going to do now?


00:52:54.440 --> 00:52:56.670
Now we ride!


00:53:01.360 --> 00:53:04.875
That means we're riding now!
This moment.

